From c37c55de4a59e8472649ad248cf2349d6de7b08f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lishuangfan13-afk <lishuangfan13@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 13:44:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(cron): add daily fixed-time schedule kind

Add a third cron schedule kind, CRON_KIND_DAILY, which fires once per
day at a fixed local hour:minute.

- cron_service.h: add CRON_KIND_DAILY and daily_hour/daily_min fields
- cron_parse_job_item(): accept kind="daily" with integer hour (0-23)
  and minute (0-59); reject out-of-range values with a clear log
- cron_save_jobs(): serialize daily as kind="daily" plus hour/minute
  (previously the every/at ternary would have written a bogus kind)
- cron_next_daily_run(): compute the next occurrence using a fixed
  UTC+8 offset + gmtime_r(), matching the convention in
  tool_get_time.c and avoiding localtime_r()/mktime() zoneinfo issues
- compute_initial_next_run(): arm daily jobs at load/add time
- cron_process_due_jobs(): advance daily jobs to the next day instead
  of treating them as one-shot or adding interval_s
- cron_service_start(): reschedule missed daily occurrences instead of
  disabling them as stale
- tool_cron.c/h: parse_daily_schedule() accepts schedule_type="daily"
  with hour/minute; update help text and list output
- tool_registry.c: document daily and hour/minute in cron_add schema
- warn and truncate deterministically when a persisted job id is
  longer than the 8-char storage buffer

Existing every/at behavior is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: yuk1-r <yuk1-r@users.noreply.github.com>
